cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SpinSlicer in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "SpinSlicer: an open-source slicer for Computed Axial Lithography"
abstract: >-
  SpinSlicer is a desktop slicer for Computed Axial Lithography (CAL), also called
  tomographic volumetric additive manufacturing (VAM). It computes projector frames
  from an STL file with a physical optics model of a rotating resin vial, simulates
  the cured part (virtual print), plans the exposure and plays the frames on the
  projector for the planned dose.
authors:
